meta {
  name: Order
  seq: 12
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Orders of the partner (the site owner), paid from its deposit. Run in this order:

  1. `Stock / List prices and stock` or `Stock / Search products`: pick `product_variation_id` with stock and its price.
  2. `Dictionary / city search` → `city_id` (KLADR), then `Delivery / calculate` with the same `items`, `country` and `city_id`: priced methods in `options`, the others in `omitted` with the reason. For a method with `type: pick_up_point` choose a point with `Delivery / pick-up-point list` (`price` — to that point) and pass it as `pick_up_point_id` to `calculate` and `Place an order`.
  3. `Order / Place an order`: the answer has the order and `deposit_due`, the amount `pay` will charge. Repeat it with the same `external_id` safely: you get the same order with `replayed: true`.
  4. `Balance / show`, then `Order / pay`: charges `deposit_due` from the deposit in `deposit_currency`.
  5. `Order / show` or `Order / list` (filter `external_id`) to follow the order; `Order / cancel` while it is not shipped. Canceling does not return the deposit: `deposit_refunded` shows what was returned.

  Environment variables used here: `productVariationId`, `deliveryMethodId`, `cityId`, `pickUpDeliveryMethodId` (set them for your site), `orderId` (filled by `Place an order`). To place an order to a pick-up point, set `delivery_method_id` to `{{pickUpDeliveryMethodId}}` and add `"pick_up_point_id"` from `Delivery / pick-up-point list`.
}
